"no record\").\n5. `content_tree` lives once, in `badf_gate.py`; `badf_compose.py` imports it (no duplicate); both behave identically on the same tree (guarded).\n6. `reconcile` remains deterministic and network-free; it reads only the object store and the tree.\n7. Each refusal branch **load-bearing** (mutation: mismatch tolerated, malformed downgraded to no-record, `composition_verified` written true without a record).\n8. `pull-request-integration` registered `IMPLEMENTED` C1 `allowed_tools: []` with a real digest; root stays `DESIGNED`; no new script, no schema change (the two new keys ride in the existing free-form `external_target`), no authority change; `repo` clean; full suite + compose green in CI.\n9. **This PR is its own subject twice:** it carries a composition record (GIT-E), and the *next* WP's reconcile of it must write `composition_verified: true` — the first landed-content verification on real history.\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_badf_git_integration.py`, the reconcile fixture pattern: scratch clone, a squash simulated on `origin/<default>`)\n\n- `test_reconcile_verifies_landed_content_against_the_record`\n- `test_reconcile_refuses_a_landing_whose_content_moved`\n- `test_reconcile_without_a_record_writes_composition_verified_false`\n- `test_reconcile_refuses_a_malformed_record_rather_than_downgrading`\n- `test_content_tree_has_one_home_and_compose_imports_it`\n- `test_reconcile_is_deterministic_and_reads_only`\n- `test_pull_request_integration_subskill_registered_and_root_stays_designed`\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Any gate code that talks to GitHub (rulesets, checks, approvals via API) — the gate stays deterministic and offline; platform observations are the procedure's, made with `gh`.\n- Approval-freshness *enforcement* (the repo runs under a single collaborator; C-1 stays open and recorded); merge queues; release tags — **GIT-H**.\n- Recovery automation for a `BLOCKED` reconcile — **GIT-G** (the procedure opens recovery; nothing rewrites `main`).\n- Th